<title>USA: Alliance Bancorp votes $0.10/shr payout.</title>
<headline>Alliance Bancorp votes $0.10/shr payout.</headline>
<dateline>HINSDALE, Ill. 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliance Bancorp, holding company for Liberty Federal Bank, said Friday its board voted a quarterly cash dividend of $0.10 per share, to be paid April 18 to holders of record as of March 31.</p>
<p>It said this is consistent with the company's previously announced intention to pay a cash dividend at an annual rate of $0.65 per share after completion of the merger of Liberty Bancorp Inc into Hinsdale Financial Corp (which subsequently changed its name to Alliance Bancorp).</p>
<p>The merger occurred February 10. Prior to the merger, Liberty Bancorp paid a $0.06 per share dividend on February 9.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
